eak holding on this specific board because any pair in the opponent\'s hand (33, 55, 77+), or any card matching the board (4, K, A, 6) will make a better Two Pair or Trips. The game history shows checks on the Pre-flop, Flop, and Turn. This passivity suggests the opponent likely does not have a strong hand (like a 6 or K), but the River Ace is a scare card. If I bet, hands that I beat (missed straight draws, high cards like Q-J) will simply fold, while any hand that beats me (Ax, Kx, 4x, Pocket Pairs) will call. Therefore, there is no value in betting. Checking allows me to see the showdown cheaply and win against the opponent\'s "air" hands.\n\nReason: My hand has showdown value against unpaired hands but is unlikely to get called by worse hands if I bet. Checking minimizes loss against better hands while securing the pot against weaker hands.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
