ad in the match, there is no need to take a high-variance spot with a weak hand.\n\nReason: I hold a very weak hand (Pair of Aces with 10 kicker) that loses to any King, Queen, Jack, 8, or pocket pair. The opponent's large bet on the river signals strength or a polarized bluff, but I do not beat enough of their range to justify a call, especially given the pot odds.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
